"""fakeclaude: a pretend Claude Code session, for show.

Everything is scripted and runs locally: no network, no API calls, no tokens.
It draws Claude Code's screen and works through made-up tasks in a made-up project.

  fakeclaude [--project N] [--manual]

  --project N  pick the made-up project (0-35: six projects, each under six repo names); random if omitted
  --manual     only work on prompts you type (by default it also invents its own)

Type a prompt and press Enter and it "works" on it. Esc interrupts. Ctrl+C twice quits.

Environment variables (all optional):
  FAKECLAUDE_HOME     home folder shown in the header (default: yours); projects appear under <home>/code
  FAKECLAUDE_MODEL    model name (default "Opus 5.5")
  FAKECLAUDE_EFFORT   effort level (default "xhigh")
  FAKECLAUDE_PLAN     plan name (default "Claude Max")
  FAKECLAUDE_VERSION  version shown (default: your installed Claude Code's, else 2.1.310)
  FAKECLAUDE_SPEED    pacing; 1.5 is twice as fast as the default 0.75
"""
